    "background_story": "Deep in the Amazon rainforest, there lived a leech named Kendra. She belonged to the hirudinea class, infamous for their blood-sucking habits. However, Kendra was different. She had a unique gift \u2013 the ability to sense the medicinal properties of the forest's creatures. Kendra would attach herself to wounded animals, not to feed, but to absorb and analyze their conditions. She could then secrete a special enzyme that accelerated their healing process. The other forest dwellers, initially wary of Kendra's kind, soon came to revere her as a guardian of health. Her hirudinea heritage, once a curse, became a blessing as she used her powers to nurture and protect the delicate balance of the rainforest ecosystem.",
